Fix broken configure check for ParaStationMPI when testing for CUDA support in UCC.
The first argument for AC_LANG_PROGRAM is missing an additional layer of braces,
while the second argument defines a main which is automatically added by AC_LANG_PROGRAM.

This fails the test with NVHPC, and might produce unexpected results with other compilers.

Author: Jan Reuter (j.reuter@fz-juelich.de)

diff -Naur psmpi-5.13.0-1.orig/mpich2/src/mpid/common/ucc/subconfigure.m4 psmpi-5.13.0-1/mpich2/src/mpid/common/ucc/subconfigure.m4
--- psmpi-5.13.0-1.orig/mpich2/src/mpid/common/ucc/subconfigure.m4	2025-09-26 10:29:11.000000000 +0200
+++ psmpi-5.13.0-1/mpich2/src/mpid/common/ucc/subconfigure.m4	2025-10-17 10:34:57.817376570 +0200
@@ -24,14 +24,12 @@
         ucc_info_defs=$(${ucc_info_path} -b)
         AC_LANG_PUSH([C])
         AC_COMPILE_IFELSE(  [AC_LANG_PROGRAM(
-                                    [${ucc_info_defs}],
+                                    [[${ucc_info_defs}]],
                                     [[
-                                        int main() {
-                                          #if !defined(HAVE_CUDA) || HAVE_CUDA != 1
-                                          #error macro not defined
-                                          #endif
-                                          return 0;
-                                        }
+                                      #if !defined(HAVE_CUDA) || HAVE_CUDA != 1
+                                      #error macro not defined
+                                      #endif
+                                      return 0;
                                     ]]
                                     )
                             ],[
